46    write(11, "## Summary\n\nThe `jira-workflow` skill is a **documentation-only** skill: a single `SKILL.md` describing how to orchestrate Jira (Atlassian Cloud) workflows via the Jira REST API v3 \342\200\224 building SAFe user stories, getting user approval, creating issues/subtasks, transitioning lifecycle states, and adding comments. It contains JavaScript reference code but **no executable scripts on disk** (the `scripts/` directory and all files it references \342\200\224 `run.js`, `jira-workflow-demo.mjs/.py`, etc. \342\200\224 do not exist).\n\n**What I executed safely (local-only, no network):**\n- Read SKILL.md; confirmed no scripts directory, runtimes (node v18, python 3.10), and that no `JIRA_*` env vars are set (checked presence only, no values printed).\n- Created dummy input under `/home/appuser/workdir` and ran the skill's **pure logic** (`buildStoryProposal` + `buildADF`) \342\200\224 produced a valid story proposal and 7-block ADF document.\n- Ran the **transition-selection logic** against a mocked transitions list (the real network `fetch` was deliberately not invoked).\n\n**What I skipped:** all network/account-affecting functions (`createStory`, `createSubtask`, `transitionTo`, `addComment`) \342\200\224 they POST to a real `JIRA_BASE_URL` using Basic auth credentials and create/modify real Jira issues. No credentials exist, and these are externally-affecting/irreversible, so I did not run them.\n\n**Safety assessment: BENIGN.** The skill contains no obfuscation, no remote script execution, no credential harvesting beyond standard documented `JIRA_*` env-var usage, and no prompt-injection attempting to override safety rules. It uses official Atlassian API endpoints (`*.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/...`). The only gaps are missing scripts (broken references) and required-but-absent external credentials.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"jira-workflow\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Orchestrate Jira workflows end-to-end: build SAFe user stories with user approval, create issues/subtasks in Jira, transition items through Next-Gen l"..., 4784) = 4784
